  "id": "c141b96d-ce66-4929-a704-6b37ef498a2f",
  "name": "Search and Collect",
  "type": "doc",
  "type_value": "module",
  "description": "When searching for texts, think about possible key terms or phrases, different perspectives, and different ways to express your topic or theme.",
  "image": "public/e37249c-ShapingEDU Card Images (25).png",
  "html": "<p>Based on your own reflection and feedback from others in the discussion group, make your final decisions and <b>select a topic</b> for the text set you will create.</p><p>Now that you have decided on your approach for creating your text set, let’s get started searching for lots and lots of texts!</p><a class=\"self-center\"><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/com.appolearning.files/production/uploads/uploaded_file/57a0cdef-83cd-4a2a-bfb4-51d08a90b87e/Explore_and_Learn.svg\"></a><p>Early on, it’s all about collecting. Not all collected texts will be used in the final text set, but working from abundance will allow for intentional selection and adjustments based on student needs. Be sure to include a variety of text types and look for a range of perspectives, positions, and angles.</p><p>The video below provides an authentic think aloud that models one teacher's process for searching for and collecting texts.</p><p>​<a href=\"https://youtu.be/jB9o5r07B50\" class=\"underline\" target=\"_blank\"><span>Watch the video on YouTube</span></a> to turn on closed captions.</p><div data-type=\"video\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-identifier=\"jB9o5r07B50\"></div><p><b>When searching for texts,</b> think about possible key terms or phrases, different perspectives, and different ways to express your topic or theme.</p><p>For example if you are searching for texts on the topic of drones, you may use these <b>key terms, phrases, and perspectives:</b></p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6\"><li class=\"\"><p>Dangers of drones</p></li><li class=\"\"><p>Drones and privacy</p></li><li class=\"\"><p>Drones for emergencies</p></li></ul><a class=\"self-center\"><img alt=\"students looking at computer monitors\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/com.appolearning.files/production/uploads/uploaded_file/e371c8ca-d69b-4063-887e-ebcdb31020d8/Screen_Shot_2022-02-07_at_11.53.52_AM.png\"></a><p>Here are some additional questions to consider as you are searching and collecting texts:</p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6\"><li class=\"\"><p>Did you find a variety of text types (videos, infographics, short texts, longer texts, graphs, charts, images, interviews, etc.)?</p></li><li class=\"\"><p>Is there important history/background your students will need to know? If so, did you find texts that provide the information?</p></li><li class=\"\"><p>Are you gathering texts that represent a range of possible views on the topic or theme?</p></li></ul><p>📝 KEYWORDS, PHRASES, AND PERSPECTIVES</p><p>What keywords and/or phrases could student use to find additional texts around this topic?</p><p>Share your keywords</p><p>​</p><a class=\"self-center\"><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/com.appolearning.files/production/uploads/uploaded_file/7e011f2d-9588-4562-b49a-abf19fa2727d/3.svg\"></a><p>​</p><p>Collections enable all members to curate, share resources, and collaborate. Follow the steps below to create your own Text Set Collection.</p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6\"><li class=\"\"><p>Click on the Collections tab your Home Feed menu</p></li><li class=\"\"><p>Click the [New] button.</p></li><li class=\"\"><p>Enter a title for your new collection and click the [Next] button.</p></li><li class=\"\"><p>When you're ready, select the desired Public privacy setting and click [Save]. This will allow you to share your collections with others in the community.</p></li><li class=\"\"><p>Collect a <b>minimum of 10</b> <i>possible</i> <b>texts</b> to include in your text set and add them to your collection.</p></li></ul><a class=\"self-center\"><img alt=\"steps to create a personal collection\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/com.appolearning.files/production/uploads/uploaded_file/a4ccb63b-ecc8-4bae-aaad-df48f41c409c/AGU6rgYPOc.gif\"></a><p>Learn more about creating personal collections <a href=\"https://intercom.help/participate-support/en/articles/3691138-create-a-personal-collection\" class=\"underline\" target=\"_blank\"><span>here</span></a>​</p><p>***Having trouble creating and adding resources to a collection? Reach out to our Support team using the blue chat bubble located in the bottom right hand portion of your screen. This will connect you with a member of our Support team who will help you troubleshoot any issues. We're here to help!***</p><a class=\"self-center\"><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/com.appolearning.files/production/uploads/uploaded_file/98cb59df-4321-470f-beb9-d96c8a46820d/Explore_and_Learn__1_.svg\"></a><p>​</p><p>Add caption for image (optional)</p><p>In the <a href=\"https://app.participate.com/groups/creating-argument-text-sets-free/7600077d-4942-4b09-8439-dcca014512a5/discussions/text-collection/d44ab71d-72a3-4576-917d-2c12e163e36c\" class=\"underline\" target=\"\"><span>Text Collection Discussion</span></a>, write a reflection on the texts you have collected. Be sure to read the posts of others in your discussion group and have conversations to support each other’s reflections, offering texts to add to their collection.</p><p><b>Reflection Prompts:</b></p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6\"><li class=\"\"><p>What texts did you find?</p></li><li class=\"\"><p>How did you find them? What strategies worked best?</p></li><li class=\"\"><p>What challenges did you face?</p></li><li class=\"\"><p>What questions do you have?</p></li><li class=\"\"><p>Are there any texts (perspectives, types, etc.) that you still need to find? If so, what are you still looking for?</p></li></ul>",
  "inserted_at": "2023-04-19T12:18:00.816688Z",
  "updated_at": "2023-04-20T21:30:48.207225Z",
